N.286="comment"*141x-14*34x42<M>
C="{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}}
\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\fs22 CTRL_setFlag_enableCtrl(ctrlHandle, true);\\par
will start either identifying the motor, or recalibrating the motor, or running the motor in closed loop. If you are bypassing all the motor identification, and also bypassing Rs recalibration and offsets recalibration, then you need to set the proper flags as follows:\\par
 \\par
        // enable the use of motor parameters being loaded from user.h\\par
        CTRL_setFlag_enableUserMotorParams(ctrlHandle,true);\\par
 \\par
        // disable Rs recalibration during motor startup\\par
        EST_setFlag_enableRsRecalc(obj->estHandle,false);\\par
 \\par
        // disable automatic calculation of bias values\\par
        CTRL_setFlag_enableOffset(ctrlHandle,false);\\par
 \\par
        // disable automatic calculation of bias values\\par
        CTRL_setFlag_enableCtrl(ctrlHandle, true);\\par
}
"
